I’ve focused on the PMP checker itself (where the real “cross‐boundary” gap lives) plus the two places it’s used (instruction and data fetch), and the shared package where the helper definitions live. Those four files will need edits so that any multi‐byte access (instruction fetch or data) is split or at least rechecked on the top‐end address.

```
// hw/ip/ibex/rtl/ibex_pmp.sv
// hw/ip/ibex/rtl/ibex_if_stage.sv
// hw/ip/ibex/rtl/ibex_mem_stage.sv
// hw/ip/ibex/rtl/ibex_pkg.sv
```
